# ⚠️  KEY ROTATION:
#    1. On your LOCAL machine (where you have the unencrypted key):
#       chezmoi encrypt ~/.ssh/tower_id_rsa > dotfiles/private_dot_ssh/tower_id_rsa.age
#    2. Commit the new .age file to your dotfiles repo
#    3. Old encrypted key is now invalid — remove it from repo history if needed:
#       git filter-branch --index-filter 'git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch <file>' HEAD
#
# ⚠️  IF THE KEY IS COMPROMISED:
#    1. Generate a new key: ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f ~/.ssh/tower_id_rsa -C "comment"
#    2. Add the new public key to the remote server (tower)
#    3. Encrypt the new private key with chezmoi (step 1 above)
#    4. Commit the new .age file
#    5. Remove the old .age file from the repo
